    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0597" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/3335e</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Moscow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. For Robins: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>15158–10095.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d505-f1"/> Under all circumstances
                            consider desirable that you come home for consultation. We are very
                            reluctant, however, to withdraw entire Red Cross Commission,
                            anticipating that there will be many opportunities to help distribution
                            food and other Red Cross relief measures next two months. Must leave
                            decision in your <pb facs="0598" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/> hands, for you
                            alone can judge possibilities of personal welfare members commission,
                            also likelihood continuing service, but all here feel that Red Cross
                            will find much valuable relief work to do and hope you before leaving
                            will find possible arrange for sufficient personnel to remain and if you
                            desire we will endeavor send other Red Cross representatives to help in
                            maintaining Red Cross efforts. Position in Russia founded on fine basis
                            already established. Cable promptly. Davison.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d505-f1" n="1" xml:id="d505-f1-content">
                <p>These are Red Cross serial numbers. On the file copy of the telegram is also
                    noted: “Sent at request of American National Red Cross.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
